  "body": "Follow-up of #4338 (U12 of #3663, the holder form).\n\n## What happens\n\nThe holder form of a user holder edits the taper, the clamp, the clamping range, the gauge length and the nose and largest diameters. The outline is the holder library outline of these values. The form cannot edit the outline point by point, and it cannot take the outline from a STEP model. A holder whose outline is not a library outline opens in the generic component editor (name only).\n\n## Expected (mockup screen 5)\n\n- **Edit outline…** opens the outline points of a user holder for an edit. Each edit is an undoable command. Every tool that uses the holder derives again in the same undo step.\n- **Import model (STEP)…** takes the outline from a STEP model of the holder (as `convert_tool_step_to_profile` does for a tool).\n- Safety: the holder outline feeds the collision checks. An edited or imported outline must never be smaller than the steel. A refusal names the point or the value.\n\n## Done means\n\n- Tests for an outline edit (lands, undoes, the tools that use the holder change in one step), a STEP import, and a refusal.\n",
